# Protected cleaned files

These paths were stabilized. Do not casually rewrite them while vibe-coding.

## Protected paths

- `packages/app/components/elements/grid.js`
- `packages/app/components/elements/grid/**`
- `packages/app/components/form-fields/**`
- `packages/app/ui/molecules/objects/**`
- `packages/app/components/menu-items/**`
- `packages/app/components/units/content-list/**`
- `packages/app/components/units/profile-list/**`
- `packages/app/ui/atoms/image.js`
- `packages/app/ui/atoms/image.web.js`

Not included: `smart-grid*` (separate from `grid`); `packages/app/lib/image-helpers.js` (optimizer URL helpers, not the atom).

## Upstream (this monorepo)

### On `main` / `master`

1. Prefer **not** editing protected paths.
2. If the task seems to require them: **stop** and **strongly recommend** creating a dedicated feature branch first.
3. Do not edit protected files on `main`/`master` unless the user explicitly overrides after that recommendation.

### On a feature branch (not `main`/`master`)

- Editing protected files is allowed when the task requires it.
- Keep changes minimal and focused; do not drive-by refactor unrelated parts.

## Child / fork / client repos

- In general, change **only** `packages/app/customization/` (and designated custom config hooks).
- Do not edit protected paths (or other shared `packages/app` logic) in forks unless the user explicitly asks and work is on a feature branch — still prefer customization overrides (maps, settings, wrappers) when possible.

## When blocked

Explain that the path is protected, urge a feature branch (upstream) or customization-only changes (forks), and wait for confirmation before editing.
